@* =============================================================================
   _ViewImports.cshtml — applies to ALL views in this folder and sub-folders.
   Loaded once; settings cascade down the directory hierarchy.
   =============================================================================

   @using directives:
     Make namespaces available without fully qualifying types inside Razor views.
     With ImplicitUsings disabled, these are the only usings Razor views see.
*@
@using TagHelpers
@using TagHelpers.Models
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Rendering

@* =============================================================================
   @addTagHelper — REGISTERING TAG HELPERS

   Syntax: @addTagHelper  TypePattern,  AssemblyName
     TypePattern   — "*" (all) or a fully-qualified class name
     AssemblyName  — the assembly that contains the tag helper classes
                     (NOT the namespace; matches the .csproj / .dll name)

   Line 1: Register ALL built-in ASP.NET Core tag helpers.
     Assembly: Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
     Includes: form, input, label, select, textarea, span (validation),
               anchor (a), environment, img, link, script, partial, cache.

   Line 2: Register ALL custom tag helpers in THIS project's assembly.
     Assembly: TagHelpers  (from TagHelpers.csproj → TagHelpers.dll)
     Includes: AlertTagHelper, GravatarTagHelper (in TagHelpers.TagHelpers namespace).
     The assembly name is what matters — the namespace is irrelevant here.

   Tag helper name-to-class mapping:
     <alert>        → TagHelpers.TagHelpers.AlertTagHelper    (via [HtmlTargetElement])
     <img-gravatar> → TagHelpers.TagHelpers.GravatarTagHelper (via [HtmlTargetElement])
     <form>         → FormTagHelper      (overrides native HTML <form> when asp-* present)
     <input>        → InputTagHelper     (only activates when asp-for is present)
     <a>            → AnchorTagHelper    (only activates when asp-action/asp-controller present)
*@
@addTagHelper *, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers
@addTagHelper *, TagHelpers

@* =============================================================================
   @removeTagHelper — OPTING OUT OF A SPECIFIC TAG HELPER

   Syntax: @removeTagHelper  FullyQualifiedClassName,  AssemblyName

   Example: remove the FormTagHelper so <form> is treated as plain HTML
   (uncomment to activate — breaks the Forms.cshtml demo if active):

   @removeTagHelper Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers.FormTagHelper, Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.TagHelpers

   Use case: migrating an existing front-end where <form action="..."> must not be
   rewritten, or when a third-party tag helper conflicts with a built-in.

   =============================================================================
   @tagHelperPrefix — REQUIRING A PREFIX ON ALL TAG HELPERS

   Syntax: @tagHelperPrefix  prefix:

   Example: @tagHelperPrefix  th:
   After this, <th:form asp-action="..."> works; plain <form asp-action="..."> does NOT.
   Useful in content pages that mix tag helper markup with raw HTML and need disambiguation.
   (Commented out here — would break all views in this tutorial.)

   =============================================================================
   SCOPE RULES:
   - Directives in _ViewImports.cshtml apply to views in the SAME folder and all sub-folders.
   - A _ViewImports.cshtml in Views/Demo/ would EXTEND (not replace) this file.
   - Place in the root Views/ folder to affect the entire application.
*@
